but I want to go through,

40:08.460 --> 40:09.740
and illustrate the formulas again,

40:10.880 --> 40:11.520
so this is,

40:11.620 --> 40:12.300
I'm not solving this,

40:12.380 --> 40:12.940
the smartest way,

40:13.000 --> 40:13.480
I'm solving this,

40:13.540 --> 40:14.780
the way to illustrate the formulas,

40:14.880 --> 40:15.340
in this lecture,

40:15.460 --> 40:15.640
okay,

40:16.540 --> 40:18.520
so,

40:18.780 --> 40:21.260
we have,

40:21.400 --> 40:22.620
q equals to 3,

40:23.220 --> 40:24.240
r equals to 0,

40:24.600 --> 40:25.320
and that makes,

40:25.400 --> 40:25.840
the big r,

40:25.940 --> 40:26.660
equal to 4,

40:26.660 --> 40:28.520
so,

40:28.640 --> 40:29.280
y cubed,

40:29.580 --> 40:30.580
is 1 half,

40:31.660 --> 40:32.920
times minus r,

40:33.000 --> 40:33.720
plus the square root of r,

40:33.820 --> 40:34.000
right,

40:34.200 --> 40:34.400
but,

40:34.820 --> 40:35.800
the little r is 0,

40:35.940 --> 40:36.580
so it just leaves us,

40:36.640 --> 40:37.700
1 half square root of 4,

40:38.280 --> 40:39.220
which is 2 over 2,

40:39.320 --> 40:39.820
which is 1,

40:40.620 --> 40:41.580
so y equals 1,

40:41.940 --> 40:43.320
and z is equal to minus 1,

40:43.880 --> 40:44.820
so my first solution,

40:44.940 --> 40:45.420
y plus z,

40:45.460 --> 40:45.840
is 0,

40:46.180 --> 40:47.380
and then I need to look at,

40:47.900 --> 40:49.600
omega minus omega squared,

40:49.680 --> 40:50.920
and omega squared minus omega,

40:51.780 --> 40:52.920
which end up giving me,

40:52.980 --> 40:53.660
i root 3,

40:53.880 --> 40:55.200
and minus i root 3,

40:55.920 --> 40:56.160
which,

40:56.240 --> 40:56.480
of course,

40:56.540 --> 40:57.320
we could understand,

40:57.900 --> 40:58.420
directly,

40:59.360 --> 41:00.200
through factoring,

41:00.560 --> 41:00.900
you know,

41:01.500 --> 41:03.080
if you wanted to,

41:03.700 --> 41:05.120
much like I showed you on 9,

41:06.020 --> 41:06.420
but anyway,

41:06.480 --> 41:06.980
there they are,

41:07.100 --> 41:08.720
now those are the little x's,

41:08.800 --> 41:08.880
right,

41:08.880 --> 41:09.660
those are not the solutions,

41:09.840 --> 41:10.600
to the original problem,

41:11.040 --> 41:11.900
these are the solutions,

41:12.060 --> 41:12.800
to the corresponding,

41:13.520 --> 41:14.460
depressed problem,

41:14.700 --> 41:14.980
right,

41:15.580 --> 41:16.760
and to get back,

41:16.820 --> 41:17.160
the solutions,

41:17.320 --> 41:18.140
to the original problem,

41:19.180 --> 41:20.040
put a smile on it,

41:20.340 --> 41:20.760
add 1,

41:22.120 --> 41:23.280
so turn that from,

41:23.500 --> 41:24.040
the other way,

41:25.080 --> 41:26.800
0 plus 1 is 1,

41:27.800 --> 41:29.140
1 plus i root 3,

41:29.260 --> 41:30.160
1 minus i root 3,

41:30.240 --> 41:30.760
and these,

41:31.520 --> 41:31.960
my friends,

41:32.080 --> 41:32.680
are the solutions,

41:32.680 --> 41:35.080
to x cubed,

41:35.160 --> 41:35.980
minus 3x squared,

41:36.060 --> 41:36.900
plus 6x minus 4,

41:36.940 --> 41:37.460
equal to 0,

41:37.460 --> 41:39.260
which means that,

41:39.460 --> 41:40.420
you can factor this,

41:40.520 --> 41:41.280
like this,

41:41.640 --> 41:43.060
which is also like that,

41:43.960 --> 41:44.340
so,

41:44.700 --> 41:46.900
yeah,

41:46.960 --> 41:47.400
there it is,

41:47.520 --> 41:48.220
this is a,

41:48.580 --> 41:49.900
solution to the cubic,

41:50.120 --> 41:50.340
now,

41:52.340 --> 41:55.200
the solution to the,

41:55.480 --> 41:55.920
you know,

41:56.880 --> 41:58.960
solution to the quintic,

41:59.280 --> 41:59.600
alright,

42:00.060 --> 42:01.300
is a little bit,

42:01.700 --> 42:03.240
a little bit harder,

42:03.240 --> 42:04.080
alright,

42:05.000 --> 42:05.480
in fact,

42:05.700 --> 42:05.900
so,

42:06.340 --> 42:07.020
all of these things,

42:07.100 --> 42:07.560
were found,

42:07.860 --> 42:08.340
basically,

42:08.520 --> 42:09.480
in the 1500s,

42:09.980 --> 42:10.260
and,

42:10.400 --> 42:11.640
certainly solidified,

42:11.740 --> 42:13.320
by the early 1600s,

42:14.200 --> 42:14.560
and,

42:14.640 --> 42:15.640
and then,

42:15.880 --> 42:16.600
mathematicians,

42:16.680 --> 42:17.480
were chewing on,

42:17.920 --> 42:18.520
how do you solve,

42:18.580 --> 42:19.600
so if we can solve the cubic,

42:19.740 --> 42:20.460
we can solve the,

42:20.540 --> 42:21.300
solve the quadratic,

42:21.480 --> 42:22.460
since time immemorial,

42:23.200 --> 42:23.600
and,

42:23.700 --> 42:24.980
then we solve the,

42:25.080 --> 42:25.620
the cubic,

42:26.660 --> 42:27.280
which was,

42:27.380 --> 42:27.600
you know,

42:27.740 --> 42:28.780
thought to be unsolvable,

42:28.780 --> 42:29.700
for quite some time,

42:29.820 --> 42:29.940
and,

42:29.940 --> 42:32.280
but then people came,

42:32.340 --> 42:32.960
to a solution of it,

42:33.040 --> 42:34.300
in the 1500s,

42:34.320 --> 42:35.060
something like that,

42:36.040 --> 42:36.360
and,

42:36.480 --> 42:39.240
you know,

42:39.440 --> 42:39.880
then,

42:40.660 --> 42:41.640
the quartics,

42:41.800 --> 42:42.980
followed soon thereafter,

42:43.660 --> 42:43.980
so,

42:44.120 --> 42:45.260
what about the next order,

42:45.340 --> 42:45.880
the fifth order,

42:45.960 --> 42:46.820
the quintic problem,

42:47.260 --> 42:47.540
alright,

42:48.140 --> 42:49.720
so then in the 1800s,

42:49.900 --> 42:51.240
mathematicians,

42:52.400 --> 42:53.120
and I mean,

42:53.260 --> 42:53.980
by 18th century,

42:54.080 --> 42:54.280
I mean,

42:54.280 --> 42:55.180
not the 1800s,

42:55.220 --> 42:56.120
but the 1700s,

42:56.180 --> 42:56.620
you know,

42:56.660 --> 42:57.620
1700 to 1800,

42:57.620 --> 43:00.020
people tried,

43:00.500 --> 43:02.140
to,

43:02.340 --> 43:02.680
you know,

43:02.940 --> 43:03.880
leverage these tricks,

43:03.980 --> 43:04.540
I've showed you,

43:04.660 --> 43:06.280
against the quintic problem,

43:07.380 --> 43:07.780
and,

43:08.000 --> 43:10.500
nothing quite worked,

43:10.640 --> 43:11.040
and then,

43:11.720 --> 43:11.960
you know,

43:12.040 --> 43:13.900
people looked at,

43:14.380 --> 43:15.260
all kinds of,

43:15.820 --> 43:16.040
you know,

43:16.120 --> 43:17.300
so you already seen,

43:17.460 --> 43:17.840
like in the,

43:17.860 --> 43:19.320
in the cubic case,

43:19.380 --> 43:20.040
there's kind of a,

43:20.040 --> 43:21.360
rotation of the roots,

43:21.440 --> 43:22.100
that's going on,

43:22.120 --> 43:22.280
right,

43:22.320 --> 43:22.560
like,

43:23.220 --> 43:24.120
they're all based on,

43:24.120 --> 43:24.940
that root of,

43:25.140 --> 43:25.780
you know,

43:25.780 --> 43:27.040
the roots of unity,

43:27.120 --> 43:27.580
on the circle,

43:27.700 --> 43:28.100
there's kind of,

43:28.140 --> 43:28.860
some kind of symmetry,

43:29.500 --> 43:30.800
rotating between the roots,

43:30.900 --> 43:31.160
so that,

43:31.200 --> 43:31.580
that was,

43:31.780 --> 43:32.820
some kind of idea,

43:32.920 --> 43:33.700
like that there,

43:34.360 --> 43:34.980
and you can,

43:35.180 --> 43:36.560
you can generalize this notion,

43:36.760 --> 43:37.200
to what's called,

43:37.320 --> 43:38.640
permutations of the roots,

43:39.420 --> 43:39.840
and,

43:39.960 --> 43:41.800
I think Lagrange,

43:42.160 --> 43:43.420
worked on this for decades,

43:43.800 --> 43:44.100
and,

43:44.940 --> 43:45.300
you know,

43:45.680 --> 43:46.680
tried all kinds of,

43:46.720 --> 43:47.720
different conceivable,

43:47.880 --> 43:48.540
substitutions,

43:48.660 --> 43:49.440
that you could think of,

43:49.520 --> 43:49.660
and,

43:50.340 --> 43:51.240
just nothing,

43:51.540 --> 43:52.460
quite stuck,

43:52.460 --> 43:53.800
and it became then,

43:53.960 --> 43:54.260
the,

43:54.260 --> 43:54.720
you know,

43:54.800 --> 43:55.240
the,

43:55.240 --> 43:56.500
the opinion of,

43:56.720 --> 43:57.480
mathematicians,

43:57.580 --> 43:59.060
that it was probably not possible,

43:59.060 --> 43:59.880
to find a,

44:00.380 --> 44:01.180
a general formula,

44:01.340 --> 44:02.440
formula for the quintic,

44:03.220 --> 44:04.200
and then,

44:04.320 --> 44:04.880
in the early,

44:05.100 --> 44:07.020
19th century,

44:07.160 --> 44:08.520
about 1812,

44:08.620 --> 44:09.040
or so,

44:09.680 --> 44:10.320
there was a,

44:11.000 --> 44:12.000
what's largely considered,

44:12.100 --> 44:12.820
to be flawed proof,

44:12.900 --> 44:14.080
by a fellow named Ruffini,

44:14.820 --> 44:16.500
and,

44:16.600 --> 44:17.860
I don't think,

44:17.980 --> 44:19.060
people who try to understand,

44:19.180 --> 44:19.780
the proof now,

44:19.960 --> 44:20.740
are people who,

44:20.740 --> 44:22.360
I haven't seen anybody,

44:22.360 --> 44:23.760
speak positively of that proof,

44:23.920 --> 44:25.360
algebraists that I know,

44:26.200 --> 44:27.340
but then Abel,

44:27.600 --> 44:28.040
or Abel,

44:28.420 --> 44:30.500
in about 1820 or so,

44:31.180 --> 44:32.480
gave a proof that,

44:32.560 --> 44:32.680
no,

44:32.760 --> 44:33.740
it was not possible,

44:33.960 --> 44:35.500
to find a general formula,

44:35.580 --> 44:36.720
in terms of radicals,

44:37.340 --> 44:38.780
like I gave you in this lecture,

44:39.000 --> 44:39.500
for the cubic,

44:40.340 --> 44:41.140
for the quintic,

44:41.220 --> 44:41.400
okay,

44:42.200 --> 44:44.460
and then in 1830,

44:44.780 --> 44:45.440
or so,

44:45.680 --> 44:47.180
a fellow by the name of Galois,

44:48.720 --> 44:49.220
you know,

44:49.320 --> 44:50.720
came up with what's called Galois,

44:50.740 --> 44:51.020
theory,

44:51.120 --> 44:51.820
and so it's like chapter,

44:52.280 --> 44:53.500
here's chapter 32,

44:54.000 --> 44:57.080
in Galien's abstract algebra,

44:57.180 --> 44:57.480
and if you,

44:57.500 --> 44:58.400
if you leave through here,

44:59.040 --> 44:59.260
you know,

44:59.300 --> 45:00.080
this is the end of,

45:00.220 --> 45:00.820
junior,

45:01.060 --> 45:02.160
senior level course,

45:02.320 --> 45:02.520
in,

45:02.600 --> 45:04.060
you know,

45:04.380 --> 45:05.280
abstract algebra,

45:05.660 --> 45:06.840
you can leave through here,

45:06.900 --> 45:07.200
and he'll,

45:07.720 --> 45:08.880
basically give you,

45:08.960 --> 45:10.340
a strategy for deciding,

45:10.640 --> 45:12.000
when it is possible,

45:12.080 --> 45:12.820
or not possible,

45:13.380 --> 45:14.920
to solve a quintic problem,

45:15.260 --> 45:16.420
by radicals,

45:16.420 --> 45:17.800
and,

45:17.880 --> 45:19.700
you know,

45:19.880 --> 45:21.800
it's possible to teach,

45:21.880 --> 45:22.660
undergraduates,

45:22.800 --> 45:23.340
math majors,

45:24.020 --> 45:24.760
this is a,

45:24.760 --> 45:26.000
contemporary abstract algebra,

45:26.120 --> 45:26.600
fourth edition,

45:26.760 --> 45:26.920
but,

45:27.300 --> 45:28.160
to do Galois theory,

45:28.300 --> 45:28.820
properly,

45:28.940 --> 45:29.740
it's probably like,

45:29.780 --> 45:30.780
a semester course,

45:31.340 --> 45:32.720
I teach it improperly,

45:32.760 --> 45:33.980
in about a third of a semester,

45:34.200 --> 45:35.540
in abstract algebra too,

45:36.200 --> 45:37.300
if you want to see details,

45:37.420 --> 45:38.460
you can go look at my course,

45:38.600 --> 45:38.760
but,

45:39.760 --> 45:41.200
you know,

45:41.260 --> 45:41.400
that,

45:41.400 --> 45:43.860
it turns out though,

45:43.920 --> 45:45.600
that for the fifth order problem,

45:45.720 --> 45:46.780
you can calculate something called,

45:46.860 --> 45:47.580
the Galois group,

45:47.980 --> 45:49.220
if the Galois group,

45:49.320 --> 45:49.860
is what's called,

45:49.900 --> 45:50.880
a solvable group,

45:50.920 --> 45:51.660
that means that,

45:51.760 --> 45:52.140
there's a,

45:52.440 --> 45:53.420
way to solve the,

45:53.420 --> 45:54.680
the corresponding,

45:54.880 --> 45:55.680
quintic equation,

45:55.860 --> 45:56.560
in terms of,

45:56.760 --> 45:58.260
formulas involving radicals,

45:58.880 --> 45:59.240
all right,

45:59.680 --> 46:01.020
but,

46:01.160 --> 46:01.600
on the other hand,

46:01.640 --> 46:03.060
if the Galois group,

46:03.140 --> 46:03.900
is not solvable,

46:04.480 --> 46:05.140
for example,

46:05.220 --> 46:05.940
it could be what's called,

46:06.000 --> 46:06.660
a simple group,

46:06.720 --> 46:07.340
a simple group,

46:07.340 --> 46:08.140
is not solvable,

46:08.980 --> 46:09.380
then,

46:09.560 --> 46:10.400
it is not possible,

46:10.400 --> 46:11.860
to find the solutions,

46:12.080 --> 46:12.720
to that quintic,

46:12.760 --> 46:13.640
in terms of formulas,

46:13.740 --> 46:14.580
involving radicals,

46:14.600 --> 46:15.040
in other words,

46:15.100 --> 46:15.980
there is no analog,

46:16.180 --> 46:17.220
of the quadratic equation,

46:17.340 --> 46:18.180
for such problems,

46:19.360 --> 46:19.720
so,

46:19.940 --> 46:22.240
that's a very,

46:22.440 --> 46:23.340
very interesting,

46:23.900 --> 46:24.920
turn of events,

46:25.260 --> 46:26.020
you know,

46:26.220 --> 46:27.100
that you,

46:27.200 --> 46:27.860
you can work out,

46:27.940 --> 46:28.540
n equals one,

46:28.640 --> 46:28.780
two,

46:28.920 --> 46:29.180
three,

46:29.720 --> 46:30.400
and four,

46:30.560 --> 46:31.260
and then all of a sudden,

46:31.340 --> 46:32.160
at n equals five,

46:32.520 --> 46:33.680
you can't do it anymore,

46:33.980 --> 46:35.180
in general at least,

46:35.500 --> 46:37.260
but on the other side of things,

46:37.360 --> 46:37.920
it was actually,

46:38.020 --> 46:39.520
the birth of modern group theory,

46:39.520 --> 46:41.180
the study of this problem,

46:41.320 --> 46:41.480
so,

46:42.080 --> 46:43.700
studying solutions,

46:43.840 --> 46:44.900
to polynomial equations,

46:45.080 --> 46:45.840
is one of the,

46:46.300 --> 46:48.020
the entry way points,

46:48.180 --> 46:49.000
to what's known as,

46:49.080 --> 46:50.160
what's known as group theory,

46:50.400 --> 46:51.320
or more largely,

46:51.440 --> 46:52.640
the study of abstract algebra,

46:52.640 --> 46:55.060
the other point of entry,

46:55.060 --> 46:55.860
for group theory,

46:56.140 --> 46:57.740
is in transformation groups,

46:58.660 --> 46:59.660
understanding,

47:00.120 --> 47:01.040
you know,

47:01.100 --> 47:01.940
what kind of,

47:02.840 --> 47:03.840
transformations,

47:04.400 --> 47:05.900
leave a shape unchanged,

47:06.260 --> 47:06.580
you know,

47:07.660 --> 47:09.060
how can I move,

47:09.840 --> 47:10.720
this thing around,

47:10.960 --> 47:12.020
and still have a,

47:12.220 --> 47:12.520
you know,

47:12.620 --> 47:13.760
the shape that's there,

47:13.920 --> 47:14.140
well,

47:15.020 --> 47:15.400
and,

47:15.480 --> 47:17.240
well anyway,

47:17.460 --> 47:18.380
symmetries and transformations,

47:18.560 --> 47:19.400
is the other entry way,

47:19.440 --> 47:19.820
to group theory,

47:19.820 --> 47:21.400
I think that's it for this one,

47:21.640 --> 47:21.760
so,

47:21.920 --> 47:22.260
thanks guys.

